    "proseDraft": "It was confirmed that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30 at 17:00 CT, with Lena's sections reaching Kwame by Thursday noon. Other remarks and questions were stated about ownership, format, attachments and notices, and those remain only as stated and not confirmed.\n\nConfirmed by participants\n- It was confirmed by Rosa, Kwame and Lena, with recheck passed, that the completed questionnaire goes to Brightwater procurement as a spreadsheet by Friday 2026-10-30 at 17:00 CT and Lena's sections reach Kwame by Thursday noon.\n\nStated in the meeting\n- It was stated that Kwame owns the questionnaire with return next Friday.\n- It was stated that next Friday is fine and time can be blocked for it.\n- It was stated that the speaker will do the legal and insurance sections and pass them to Kwame to merge in.\n- It was stated that the speaker will let their procurement lead know it is in progress.\n- It was stated that the speaker will double-check that it covers security documents.\n- It was stated that the speaker will then answer for both and flag it.\n- It was stated to attach the summary letter and not the full report because that needs an NDA.\n- It was stated as a question whether to attach the pen test summary or just reference it.\n- It was stated that the format is spreadsheet because the portal is being replaced.\n- It was stated as a question whether they want it in their portal or as a spreadsheet.\n- It was stated to put them in the shared folder rather than email.\n- It was stated as a question whether they want the certificate itself or just the coverage amounts.\n- It was stated that the speaker will ask when writing to procurement."
